.TH GOOGLE-PICTURE-SYNC 1 "November 2026" "0.1.0"
.SH NAME
google-picture-sync \- copy Google Drive media into yearly Google Photos albums
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B google-picture-sync
.RI [ --config " file" ] " action"
.RI [ --limit " count" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively copy images and optionally videos from four-digit year folders.
Originals are never deleted. Run from the repository directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --init
Create configuration.
.TP
.B --auth
Authorize using desktop OAuth credentials.
.TP
.B --test
Check Drive and Photos album read access.
.TP
.B --scan, --dry-run
List eligible files without uploading.
.TP
.BI --year " YYYY"
Migrate a single year.
.TP
.B --all, --resume
Migrate all eligible uncompleted media.
.TP
.B --retry-failed
Retry known failed records.
.TP
.B --status
Display local migration counts.
.TP
.B --limit
Maximum new upload attempts; zero means unlimited.
.TP
.B --help, --version
Display usage or version.
.SH FILES
.env/config.ini, .env/credentials.json, .env/token.json, .env/migration.sqlite3
.SH NOTES
Pending records are skipped to avoid duplicate uploads after uncertain API outcomes.
Do not run concurrent instances. Google passwords are not used.
